-- ── story 4-7b: blind returns — a parcel received with no RMA ───────────────
-- Generated by drizzle-kit (the column, nullability and index statements) and
-- hand-amended around the generated part: the fail-fast guard, `IF NOT
-- EXISTS` on every column and index, the CHECKs (drizzle-kit is blind to
-- CHECKs; `bun run db:generate` afterwards reports "No schema changes"), the
-- proof on data and the post-migration probe.
--
-- A blind receipt is an RMA (decision 1): the handheld's `return.receive_blind`
-- auto-creates one with `origin = 'blind'`, born `received`, whose review is
-- `pending` until an ops manager accepts (optionally linking a dispatched
-- order) or rejects it on the web. No status vocabulary widens.
--
-- `return_authorizations`:
--   * `order_id`, `order_dispatched_at` DROP NOT NULL (metadata only) — null on
--     a blind RMA until it is accepted with an order;
--   * `origin text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'authorized'` — every existing row reads
--     `authorized` (the constant default: no rewrite, PG11+);
--   * the blind columns, all NULL on an authorized RMA: `review_status`,
--     `parcel_reference`, `suggested_order_id`, `match_kind`, `client_prompted`
--     (A24), `reviewed_by`, `reviewed_at`, `review_reason_code`, `review_note`;
--   * the CHECKs, NOT VALID (guide §3 — every existing row holds them by
--     construction: `origin` is the default and every blind column NULL, which
--     the proof block below counts explicitly). A later deploy runs exactly
--     (DEPLOY.md §5):
--       ALTER TABLE "return_authorizations" VALIDATE CONSTRAINT "return_authorizations_origin_check";
--       ALTER TABLE "return_authorizations" VALIDATE CONSTRAINT "return_authorizations_review_status_check";
--       ALTER TABLE "return_authorizations" VALIDATE CONSTRAINT "return_authorizations_match_kind_check";
--       ALTER TABLE "return_authorizations" VALIDATE CONSTRAINT "return_authorizations_review_reason_code_check";
--       ALTER TABLE "return_authorizations" VALIDATE CONSTRAINT "return_authorizations_parcel_reference_length";
--       ALTER TABLE "return_authorizations" VALIDATE CONSTRAINT "return_authorizations_review_note_length";
--       ALTER TABLE "return_authorizations" VALIDATE CONSTRAINT "return_authorizations_origin_shape";
--       ALTER TABLE "return_authorizations" VALIDATE CONSTRAINT "return_authorizations_review_shape";
--       ALTER TABLE "return_authorization_lines" VALIDATE CONSTRAINT "return_authorization_lines_reason_code_check";
--     - `origin_shape`: an authorized RMA has its order and dispatch instant
--       and no blind column; a blind RMA has a review status and
--       `client_prompted`, `order_id` is NULL exactly when
--       `order_dispatched_at` is, and an order only once ACCEPTED;
--     - `review_shape`: reviewed (accepted | rejected) exactly when
--       `reviewed_by` and `reviewed_at` are set; rejected exactly when a
--       reason is; `other` needs a note; `match_kind` exactly beside
--       `suggested_order_id`. Every nullable arm is coalesced or says
--       `IS NULL OR` first (guide §3 — `NULL IN (…)` passes a CHECK).
--   * two partial indexes: the pending-review queue and (A20) blind RMAs by
--     parcel reference.
--
-- `return_authorization_lines`: `order_line_id` DROP NOT NULL (a blind line is
-- unlinked until an accept links it); the reason CHECK is dropped and re-added
-- with `unannounced` (guide §3 — the real name, 0072's, never `IF EXISTS`).
--
-- `shipments`: `(tenant_id, tracking_number)` for the AWB arm of the parcel
-- lookup. LOCK COST (A22): a plain CREATE INDEX on `shipments` holds a SHARE
-- lock for the build, blocking label and manifest writes; the migrator runs
-- the pending set in one transaction, so it cannot be CONCURRENTLY. The table
-- holds one row per labelled order and the deploy runs in the maintenance
-- window (DEPLOY.md). On a large table the deploy migrator refuses the build
-- until it is pre-built CONCURRENTLY under the same name (`IF NOT EXISTS`
-- then makes this statement a no-op — guide §3, DEPLOY.md §5).
--
-- Rolling deploy: an old (4-7a) api task reads the nullable `order_id` only
-- on blind RMAs, which only the new build writes.

-- ── 0. fail-fast: already applied, or 4-7a missing ───────────────────────
DO $$
BEGIN
	IF EXISTS (
		SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns
		 WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'return_authorizations' AND column_name = 'origin'
	) THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0112: return_authorizations.origin already exists — this migration has already been applied.';
	END IF;
	IF NOT EXISTS (
		SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns
		 WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'return_receipt_lines' AND column_name = 'open_qty'
	) THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0112: return_receipt_lines.open_qty is missing — story 4-7a''s 0097 must be applied first.';
	END IF;
END $$;
